%N A398718 Number of right-Euclidean relations on an n-element labeled set.
%C A398718 A relation R is right-Euclidean if xRy and xRz imply yRz for all x, y, z.
%F A398718 E.g.f.: exp(x + Sum_{k>=1} x^k*exp((2^k-1)*x)/k!).
%F A398718 Binomial transform of A398475.
%e A398718 For n = 2, the 7 right-Euclidean relations are {}, {(1,1)}, {(2,2)}, {(1,1),(2,1)}, {(1,2),(2,2)}, {(1,1),(2,2)}, and {(1,1),(1,2),(2,1),(2,2)}.
%Y A398718 Cf. A001831, A398475.
